   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law and the social services law, in relation to\nproviding for the inclusion of a check off box on personal income tax return\nforms for the purpose of making a gift to the William B. Hoyt Memorial\nchildren and family trust fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S2503",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2503-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §630-g, Tax L; amd §481-e, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2503\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law and the social services law, in relation to\nproviding for the inclusion of a check off box on personal income tax\nreturn forms for the purpose of making a gift to the William B. Hoyt\nMemorial children and family trust fund\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill provides for the inclusion of a check off box on personal\nincome tax forms for the purpose of making a gift to the William B. Hoyt\nMemorial Children and Family trust fund for child abuse prevention.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the tax law by adding a new section 630-g: Effective\nfor any tax year commencing on or after January 1, 2021, an individual\nin any taxable year may elect to contribute to the William B. Hoyt Memo-\nrial children and family trust fund. Such contribution shall be in any\nwhole dollar amount and shall not reduce the amount of state tax owed by\nsuch individual. The tax commission shall include space on the personal\nincome tax return to enable a taxpayer contribution. All revenues\ncollected from pursuant to this section shall be credited to the William\nB. Hoyt Memorial children and family trust fund.\n\nSection 2 amends the social services law to require a description of how\nthe funds collected were utilized during the preceding year.\n\nSection 3 sets an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder this bill taxpayers would have the option to support and strength-\nen New York children and families by donating to the William B. Hoyt\nMemorial Children and Family Trust Fund. Research shows that as the\nnumber of adverse child experiences increase, the risk for numerous long\nterm health problems increases significantly.  Investing in prevention\ncan reduce the need for costly intervention services resulting from\nabuse and maltreatment. The William B. Hoyt Memorial Children and Family\nTrust Fund is administered by the Office of Children and Families. In\n2013, 27 programs received funding from the Trust Fund which helped over\n167,554 adults and children in the state. The Trust Fund programs have\npositive outcomes for individuals served, such as: improved factors that\nprotect against child abuse and neglect improved safety for children,\nadults and elders exposed to family violence and reduced incidents of\nAbusive Head Trauma (Shaken Baby Syndrome).\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to all tax years\ncommencing on and after January 1, 2021.\n",
